-- title:
--   Cyclic Galois levels over the fixed ring of Fr^m
-- statement:
--   Let $r$ be a prime and let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring, $\pi\in\mathcal O$ irreducible, $\mathcal O$ complete for the $(\pi)$-adic topology, with residue ring of cardinality $r$ and $(r)=(\pi)$. Let $\mathcal O^{nr}$ be a characteristic-zero domain which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra, complete for the ideal $(\pi)$ generated by the image of $\pi$, with that ideal maximal, such that every element of $\mathcal O^{nr}$ satisfies some monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$ and every monic polynomial over $\mathcal O^{nr}$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$; let $\mathrm{Fr}$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism of $\mathcal O^{nr}$ with $\mathrm{Fr}\,x\equiv x^{r}\pmod\pi$. Fix $m>0$, write $S$ for the equaliser of $\mathrm{Fr}^{m}$ and the identity (the fixed subring), and let $\mathrm{Fr}_S$ be an $S$-algebra automorphism of $\mathcal O^{nr}$ acting as $\mathrm{Fr}^{m}$. Put $\mathcal O_k$ for the equaliser of $\mathrm{Fr}_S^{\,k}$ and the identity as $S$-algebra maps. Then: (i) for every $N$ and every $x\in\mathcal O^{nr}$ there are $k>0$ and $x'\in\mathcal O_k$ with $x-x'\in(\pi^{N})$; (ii) for every $k>0$ there are $\zeta\in\mathcal O_k$ and an $S$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $\mathcal O_k$ acting as $\mathrm{Fr}_S$, such that $\zeta^{0},\dots,\zeta^{k-1}$ is an $S$-basis of $\mathcal O_k$ (each element has unique coefficients $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,k\to S$), $\sigma^{i}\zeta-\sigma^{j}\zeta$ is a unit for $i\neq j$, and there is an $S$-algebra isomorphism $\mathcal O_k\otimes_S\mathcal O_k\simeq(\mathrm{Fin}\,k\to\mathcal O_k)$ sending $x\otimes y$ to $(x\,\sigma^{j}y)_j$.
--
--   This is the Teichmüller-level description of the completed maximal unramified extension: the fixed rings of the powers of Frobenius over the fixed ring of $\mathrm{Fr}^m$ form an exhaustive tower of free cyclic Galois subalgebras, with the Galois condition stated as the explicit splitting of $\mathcal O_k\otimes\mathcal O_k$. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, as the arithmetic input for descent along Frobenius for the formal upper half-plane functor (tensor-product descent of elements, of compact opens, and of maps of spectra).
